        "notes": "Eligible direct calls use tail. call ret rather than growing the .NET stack. Tail-position recognition covers direct returns, conditional branches, logical AND/OR, and object-ABI nullish-coalescing right operands and final comma operands. The new comma and nullish cases pass at the pinned tcoHelper.js depth of 100,000. Calls requiring argument objects, rest/spread handling, or function-object invocation are not eligible; constructors, async/generator functions, and protected returns retain their existing lowering."
